; =====================================================================================
; openQHA - Branch A - CREST iMTD-GC conformational search
;
; IDENTITY: this is a PROTOCOL SPECIFICATION, not a job that is run.
;   Branch A's dynamics is run by CREST, not by GROMACS. GROMACS computes nothing
;   anywhere in this repository. This file exists for one reason:
;
;       to put branch A's dynamics settings in the SAME FORMAT as branch B's, so the
;       two can be compared line by line instead of by memory.
;
;   The comparison is the point. Read this file next to s0_qha_production.mdp and the
;   incompatibility is mechanical rather than a claim you have to trust.
;
; REFERENCES:
;   iMTD-GC algorithm .... Pracht, Bohle & Grimme, Phys. Chem. Chem. Phys. 2020, 22, 7169
;   MD settings .......... Grimme, J. Chem. Theory Comput. 2019, 15, 2847
;   GFN2-xTB ............. Bannwarth, Ehlert & Grimme, JCTC 2019, 15, 1652
;   Parameters in force .. configs/conformers.yaml (crest:)
;
; =====================================================================================
; *** DO NOT RUN THIS FILE THROUGH GROMACS, AND DO NOT COPY ITS SETTINGS INTO ***
; ***                    A QUASI-HARMONIC TRAJECTORY.                        ***
; =====================================================================================
;
; Every setting below exists to CROSS BARRIERS. Each one buys sampling by destroying
; the physical thermal fluctuations:
;
;   (1) BIAS POTENTIAL. Metadynamics deliberately does not sample the Boltzmann
;       distribution of the true surface -- that is what it is for. A quasi-harmonic
;       analysis reads entropy out of the covariance of the fluctuations, and a biased
;       trajectory inflates that covariance. The eigenvalues come out too large, so
;       nu_i = sqrt(kB*T/lambda_i) comes out too low, so the entropy comes out too HIGH.
;       The direction is fixed. It is a bias, not noise, and averaging does not remove it.
;
;   (2) CONSTRAINTS. SHAKE does not soften a degree of freedom, it REMOVES it. The
;       covariance is identically zero along every constrained bond, so the 3N-6
;       non-zero eigenvalues cannot all be filled. The count itself breaks.
;
;   (3) DEUTERIUM MASS. Hydrogen at 2 amu drops the C-H stretches from about 3000 to
;       about 2200 cm^-1. Every vibrational term computed from such a trajectory is
;       wrong, and wrong by an amount that looks plausible.
;
; Any one of the three is fatal to a quasi-harmonic analysis on its own. Branch A does
; not care about any of them, because ITS PRODUCT IS A GEOMETRY, NOT A TRAJECTORY.
;
; The handover between the branches is the BASIN GEOMETRIES. Branch B restarts from
; them with dt = 1 fs, constraints = none and real hydrogen mass, and uses not one frame
; of the CREST run.
; =====================================================================================

; -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
; Integrator and timestep
; -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
; The 5 fs step is only stable because bonds are constrained AND hydrogens are heavy.
; These three settings are ONE PACKAGE. Measured, taking two of the three (shake = 1,
; H bonds only, with the 5 fs step and 2 amu mass): 29 and 20 metadynamics runs
; `terminated EARLY` on GFN2-xTB. See conformers.yaml section 1.4 for the four-arm
; attribution.
integrator               = md            ; CREST: leapfrog Verlet, its own implementation
dt                       = 0.005         ; ps  = 5 fs   (JCTC 2019, 15, 2847)
                                         ; branch B uses 0.001. That is the whole gap.

; -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
; Constraints -- REMOVED degrees of freedom, not softened ones
; -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
constraints              = all-bonds     ; CREST shake = 2, "all covalent bonds"
constraint-algorithm     = shake
shake-tol                = 1e-07         ; CREST src/dynamics/shake_module.f90:81
;
; KNOWN FAILURE MODE, and the fallback it needs. On strained rings the SHAKE iteration
; (250 iterations max, shake_module.f90:80) does not converge, do_shake returns non-zero,
; the MD is judged failed, and CREST prints `terminated EARLY` -- WITHOUT printing any
; reason. Measured:
;
;     dsgdb9nsd_000607  O[C@H]1C[C@H]1C#N    all-bonds -> 31 aborts | h-bonds -> 0
;     dsgdb9nsd_003163  O[C@H]1CC[C@]21CO2   all-bonds -> 24 aborts | h-bonds -> 0
;     dsgdb9nsd_002334  CCC[C@H]1C[C@H]1C    all-bonds ->  4 aborts | h-bonds -> 0
;
; The fallback is POINTWISE: only a molecule that actually aborted is retried, once, at
; h-bonds, in a separate directory, and marked in its own record. A molecule that fell
; back must never be mistakable for one that ran the published protocol.
;
;   constraints          = h-bonds       ; the fallback, applied per molecule, never globally

; -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
; Masses
; -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
; RECORDED, NOT SET: 2.0 amu is already CREST's own default (src/confparse.f90:215,
; env%hmass = 2.0d0). Written here so the third member of the package is visible in our
; own record instead of living only in someone else's source tree.
;
; GROMACS spells this as a topology modification rather than an .mdp key; the closest
; .mdp expression is the heavy-hydrogen flag, given here for the comparison only.
;   define                = -DHEAVY_H    ; H mass -> 2 amu (deuterium)
; branch B: real hydrogen mass, 1.008 amu. No mass repartitioning of any kind.

; -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
; Thermostat
; -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
tcoupl                   = berendsen     ; JCTC 2019, 15, 2847
tau-t                    = 0.5           ; ps
ref-t                    = 300           ; K, bath temperature
;
; NOTE the gap between bath and reality: the paper reports ACTUAL average temperatures
; of 350-500 K under the bias. That is expected for metadynamics and harmless here --
; and it is a second, independent reason this trajectory cannot be used for
; thermodynamics at 298.15 K. Branch B uses v-rescale at ref-t = 298.15 and checks that
; the realised temperature matches.

; -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
; Metadynamics bias -- the setting with no GROMACS equivalent
; -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
; This is where the .mdp analogy runs out, and the fact that it runs out is itself the
; clearest statement of why the two protocols cannot share a file. GROMACS has no key
; for "add the current structure to an RMSD-space bias potential every 1 ps". The
; published values (PCCP 2020, 22, 7169), for the record:
;
;   number of MTD runs .......... 12, with different Vbias settings
;   bias width alpha ............ 0.1 to 1.3 Bohr^-2
;   bias height k_i/N ........... 0.75 to 3.00 mEh
;   bias update ................. a new structure added every 1.0 ps
;   MTD length .................. t = 0.1*(Neff + 0.1*Neff^2), bounded 5 ps <= t <= 200 ps
;   unbiased MD ................. 2 runs, at 400 K and 500 K, on the 3 lowest conformers
;   iteration ................... restarted at least once, at most five times
;   snapshots ................... every 0.1 ps
;   energy windows (3 stages) ... 18 / 12 / 6 kcal/mol
;   GC limit .................... min(5000, t * 50 ps)
;
; branch B: NO BIAS OF ANY KIND. That is the first of the three prohibitions at the
; top of s0_qha_production.mdp.
;
; A separate protocol worth naming so it is not confused with this one: CREST's
; reactive nanoreactor uses NO SHAKE and dt = 0.2-0.5 fs, "in order to allow any
; reaction". Different goal, different settings, same program.

; -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
; Boundary conditions and interactions
; -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
pbc                      = no            ; isolated molecule, gas phase
cutoff-scheme            = group
nstlist                  = 0             ; no neighbour list: every pair, every step
coulombtype              = cut-off
rcoulomb                 = 0
rvdw                     = 0
rlist                    = 0             ; 0 = infinite in GROMACS; the semi-empirical
                                         ; Hamiltonian has no cutoff at these sizes

; -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
; Output
; -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
nstxout                  = 20            ; 20 * 5 fs = 0.1 ps, the paper's snapshot rate
nstvout                  = 0             ; velocities are not used downstream
nstenergy                = 20
nstlog                   = 200

; =====================================================================================
; The two protocols, side by side
; =====================================================================================
;
;   setting            branch A (this file)        branch B (s0_qha_production.mdp)
;   -----------------  --------------------------  ---------------------------------
;   purpose            cross barriers              sample one basin at equilibrium
;   product            geometries                  a trajectory
;   bias               metadynamics, 12 runs       NONE
;   dt                 5 fs                        1 fs
;   constraints        all-bonds (SHAKE)           none
;   hydrogen mass      2 amu (deuterium)           real, 1.008 amu
;   thermostat         Berendsen, tau 0.5 ps       v-rescale
;   ref-t              300 K (realised 350-500 K)  298.15 K, and checked
;   potential          GFN2-xTB, MACE refines      MACE only
;   what may be read   which minima exist          frequencies, entropy, free energy
;   off the result
;
; Read the last two rows together. Branch A's trajectory cannot tell you a frequency;
; branch B's cannot tell you which minima exist. Neither is a deficiency -- they are
; different instruments, and the only error available here is using one for the other.
; =====================================================================================
